From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] iokit: share the virtio transport between NeoDarwin's virtio drivers

P1-19 adds a second virtio driver, NeoDarwinVirtioNet, next to P1-10's
NeoDarwinVirtioBlock. What both need of the modern PCI transport
(virtio 1.2 §4.1.4: the vendor capabilities, reset, status, feature
negotiation, queue set-up, MSI-X vectors) and of split virtqueues (§2.7)
moves out of the block driver into kernel/neodarwin/virtio, overlaid at
iokit/ndvirtio: nd_virtio.h (the layouts) and NeoDarwinVirtioPCI.h (the
transport and the ring, header-only). The block device's own layouts stay
in kernel/neodarwin/storage (nd_virtio_blk.h). This patch gives the block
driver the new directory's search path (docs/kernel/storage.md,
docs/kernel/network.md).

Rebase-risk: low (an appended make variable; applies after 0033).
---
--- a/iokit/conf/Makefile.template
+++ b/iokit/conf/Makefile.template
@@ -120,6 +120,11 @@ NeoDarwinVirtioBlock.cpo_CFLAGS_ADD += -I$(ND_STORAGE)
 NeoDarwinVirtioBlock.cpo_CFLAGS_ADD += -I$(ND_STORAGE) -I$(ND_STORAGE)/include -I$(ND_PCI) -I$(ND_IOPCI) \
 	-I$(ND_PCI)/compat -I$(SRCROOT)/libkern/ndpthread/compat -Wno-deprecated-declarations
 
+# The virtio transport NeoDarwin's virtio drivers share (patch 0034):
+# kernel/neodarwin/virtio, overlaid at iokit/ndvirtio, header-only.
+ND_VIRTIO = $(SRCROOT)/iokit/ndvirtio
+NeoDarwinVirtioBlock.cpo_CFLAGS_ADD += -I$(ND_VIRTIO)
+
 # NeoDarwin's NVMe driver (patch 0029): the controller on an IOPCIDevice and
 # its namespaces' IOBlockStorageDevices, with the same headers.
 $(foreach o,NeoDarwinNVMeController.cpo NeoDarwinNVMeNamespace.cpo,$(eval $(o)_CFLAGS_ADD += -I$(ND_STORAGE) \
